897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:38:24-08:00","id":753017,"title":"","content":"It's your game, don't understand the hard on for the skull pig but it's your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:24:09-08:00","id":753059,"title":"","content":"Just spitballing- but since you really want to use a skullpig, what if the skullpig was rooting around and it found the Wyrm orifice that leads to the Black Spiral, and it is the one that gets the corruption ball rolling among the White Howlers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:39:23-08:00","id":753619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/752067-ideas-for-white-howler-game?p=753059#post753059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just spitballing- but since you really want to use a skullpig, what if the skullpig was rooting around and it found the Wyrm orifice that leads to the Black Spiral, and it is the one that gets the corruption ball rolling among the White Howlers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I've actually been looking at this thread for a couple of days now and really wanting to engage but fussing over having too little time for a proper response. I'd love to combine that idea with the Skullpig(s) being a red herring. The Skullpigs are a roving menace - they are going around and messing things up, but they are not the true problem for the sept<br /> <br /> Prince of Night suggested that the local sept is Shadow Lord led and that the key conflict would be between them and civilisation encroaching. I'd love to play that up with a noteable Roman settlement being built around a local thermal well and a crucial road connecting two parts of the empire. This city has a number of Roman and British Warders of Men who are building a guarded alliance with the sept and hope to create a Caern within the city or join the sept full time. Their relationships are compounded by the local legion being under control of a vampire (maybe your Salubri triumvirate has founded this city with the hope of creating their own area free of the other clans?) or a wyrm corrupted legion leader?<br /> <br /> The xenophobia and conflict are everywhere, and the Warders and the Lords are stuck in the middle, with a corrupt government running the city and the Skullpigs roving around the sept and city causing havoc. Let's say that a proud Shadow Lord Hero decides he has enough. He decides to bargain with disease spirits and offers them too much - the City is struck by a horrifying plague murdering most of the populace and turning the rest into fomori.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the Warders and the Lords are pitted against each other. Who is to blame? Why did all the innocents die unnecesarily? Will they murder each other? Who will stop all the roving fomori who are being shepherded by the Skullpigs into a force that could destroy the Caern? What will the Shadow Lord Hero do to hide his involvement? When he is uncovered will he run for the hills and eventually take the Wyrm's offer of salvation and take over the fomori and the skullpigs?<br /> <br /> That is the question for the player pack to resolve. Bonus points if it's a mixed one, and if you spend the first couple of sessions establishing everything and getting people into a confident groove and introducing them to all the players before things start truly going to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value